  "author": "/root",
  "source_review": {
    "review": "Scalar instruction execution is related to actual legal traces and charged cost. The fixed copy program copies each actual source cell and preserves outside memory under the literal nonoverlap hypotheses, with halt/cost at most6N+2. The fixed header decoder uses only castNat, equalReal, increment and halt; every legal trace from its stated loop state returns the supplied natural at3n+3 with that cost bound and unchanged memory.",
    "limits": "The decoder assumes real register0 already contains the cast natural header. Loading an InputMemory header, assembling callers and bounding an entire algorithm remain separate. It makes no termination claim for arbitrary nonnatural real headers."
  },
